    "scientific_verdict": "Across k in {1, 2, 3} oracle calls, the two-copy coherent SWAP expectation excess between same-secret and independent-secret pairs equals the full operator Hilbert-Schmidt variance V_HS(epsilon, sigma) = 1 - Tr(rho_bar^2) (which is invariant under flipping sigma_k -> -sigma_k and equals 1 - |V_{epsilon_1}(f)|/D^2 for k = 1), whereas post-Fourier modular CNOT difference readout has coincidence excess at Delta = 0 equal to the computational-basis L2 signal energy E_{epsilon, sigma} <= V_HS(epsilon, sigma)."
  },
  "theorems": [
    {
      "id": "T1",
      "name": "Coherent Same-Secret vs Independent-Secret SWAP Identity",
      "statement": "For any k-call schedule (epsilon, sigma), Tr(S_D * E_s[rho(s) tensor rho(s)]) = 1 and Tr(S_D * (rho_bar tensor rho_bar)) = Tr(rho_bar^2), so the two-copy SWAP expectation excess equals the operator Hilbert-Schmidt variance V_HS(epsilon, sigma) = 1 - Tr(rho_bar^2) and the independent-pair antisymmetric projector probability equals V_HS / 2."
    },
    {
      "id": "T2",
      "name": "Final-Fourier Direction Invariance of Purity and Exact 1-Call Collision Variety Law",
      "statement": "The ensemble purity Tr(rho_bar_(epsilon, sigma)^2) = ||M_hat_(epsilon, sigma)(0)||_F^2 is invariant under flipping sigma_k -> -sigma_k, and for k = 1 it equals |V_(epsilon_1)(f)| / D^2 independently of the error table e."
    },
    {
      "id": "T3",
      "name": "Exact Harmonic Autocorrelation Law and Two-Copy Coincidence Excess Identity",
      "statement": "Under modular CNOT difference readout Delta = (x_2 - x_1) mod D on two same-secret copies, E_s[P_diff(Delta | s)] = sum_x C(0; x) C(0; x + Delta) + sum_(delta != 0) sum_x C(delta; x) conj(C(delta; x + Delta)), and at Delta = 0 the coincidence excess E_s[P_diff(0 | s)] - sum_x C(0; x)^2 equals E_(epsilon, sigma) <= V_HS(epsilon, sigma)."
    }
  ],
  "title": "Native Higher-Call Two-Copy SWAP Purity Bridge: Coherent SWAP Excess vs Classical Coincidence Excess, 1-Call Variety Purity Law, and CNOT Autocorrelation Equivalence"
}
